From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] gallium: d3d9umd, a Direct3D 9 user-mode driver on gallium nine

A WDDM Direct3D 9 user-mode driver (D3DDDI, OpenAdapter) for virtio-gpu, built as viogpu_d3d9.dll
(-Dgallium-d3d9umd=true -Dgallium-d3d9-dll-name=...). The Microsoft D3D9 runtime keeps the API, swapchains and
presentation; the driver implements the DDI on a headless gallium nine device over the virgl GDI winsys.

- frontends/d3d9umd: the DDI side (C++, WDK headers: adapter, caps, device, pipeline, generated DDI stubs) and
  nine_bridge.c (C, nine's D3D9 headers), which maps DDI resources/state/draws onto nine objects. System memory
  resources wrap the runtime's memory; the runtime's lock notifications invalidate nine's uploads.
- gdikmt: create a device on an adapter LUID (the D3D9 driver probes the virtio-gpu adapter at OpenAdapter).
- nine: builds with MSVC (VLAs, void * arithmetic, GNU variadic macros, Linux-only allocator and threadpool code);
  a headless device without a present group; buffers on external memory; system memory surfaces keep the memory
  they are given; NineBeforeDraw/NineAfterDraw exported; a user_constbufs driver cap (virgl only reads constant
  buffer 0 when it is user data).

Development tracing: create C:\viogpu_d3d9_trace.txt and every DDI call is logged to C:\viogpu_d3d9_trace.log.
---
